;; persisted.scm — what you told the editor to remember.
;;
;; the repl appends here: a form whose head is in `phosphor/persistent-heads`
;; (repl.scm) is written to this file after it runs, which is 6b's
;; `⇒ #ok · persisted to …`. 7a's always-allow rule lands here too.
;;
;; it is yours to edit. delete a line to unbind it; there is nothing else in it.
;;
;; it loads last, and that is the whole reason it exists rather than the forms
;; going into init.scm — see repl.scm's `phosphor/persist-file`.
